  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Lakr233/vphone-cli/zipball/2.6.1",
  "body": "## vphone 2.6.1\n\n**Core Bundle**\n- iPhone18,1 and iPhone18,2 (iPhone 17 Pro and 17 Pro Max) boot iOS 27. Their iOS 27 dyld cache is larger than the cloudOS 26.4 guest kernel's 6 GiB shared region, so it could not map and launchd panicked on first boot. The new kernel patch `kernel-boot-shared_region_size` widens the region to 7 GiB. It is boot-essential for iOS 27 and reaches an existing machine through `cfw update-kernel` followed by `cfw install`. (#599, #596)\n- `cfw install` refuses a dyld cache that does not fit the guest kernel's shared region, and names both sizes, instead of finishing a guest that panics on first boot. (#599)\n- Opening the camera no longer freezes the VM. The virtual camera's code patcher now stops cameracaptured's other threads while it rewrites a page, so its XPC threads no longer crash on a page that is briefly not executable. (#598)\n- Compiler warnings are fixed. (#597)\n\n**Launchpad**\n- No changes. Keep using the notarized Launchpad 2.6.0; the `vphone-launchpad-2.6.1.zip` built by CI is the same app, unsigned.\n\n**Upgrading**\n\nLaunchpad 2.6.0 works with any `VPhone.bundle` 2.6.x and installs this one from Core Bundle. Move your machines to it with **Change Core Bundle\u2026**. For an iPhone18,1 or iPhone18,2 machine on iOS 27 that did not boot, stop it, choose **Update Kernel** in the inspector's Patches section, then **Change Core Bundle\u2026** with **Update guest environment** on.\n"
